 succeeded in 0ms:
IndyDevDan/book/vol-1-tac/06-let-your-agents-focus.html:282:          <p>A single session reads the issue, explores the repository, debates three plan options, implements one, sees noisy test logs, makes repairs, summarizes a diff, opens a browser, captures screenshots, writes docs, and prepares a pull request. The window contains an impressive amount of information. It also contains abandoned ideas, obsolete file states, tool noise, and instructions for responsibilities that conflict.</p>
IndyDevDan/book/vol-1-tac/06-let-your-agents-focus.html:312:          <p>This nuance prevents the most tempting misread. A review prompt may contain setup, variables, diff instructions, screenshot policy, severity guidelines, and a strict JSON schema. That is substantial work. It is still one purpose because every instruction exists to answer spec conformance with proof.</p>
IndyDevDan/book/vol-1-tac/06-let-your-agents-focus.html:385:          <p>The state file shown during planning contains the ADW ID, issue number, branch name, plan file, and issue class. As phases finish, those fields become a compact routing packet. The reviewer can load state, check out the right branch, and find the spec. It does not need the planner’s internal conversation. The documenter can find the same spec and review screenshots from state without inheriting the reviewer’s reasoning trace.</p>
IndyDevDan/book/vol-1-tac/06-let-your-agents-focus.html:467:            <figcaption><span class="frame-card__t">21:45</span>The prompt’s JSON shape and the code’s Pydantic shape line up. A run does not merely produce prose; it produces a comparable record.</figcaption>
IndyDevDan/book/vol-1-tac/06-let-your-agents-focus.html:482:          <ol><li>Preserve the branch state in which Export is misplaced.</li><li>Run <code>uv run adws/adw_review.py &lt;issue#&gt; &lt;adw-id&gt; --skip-resolution</code> and save the returned review data.</li><li>Through the agentic workflow, add the instruction that every captured image must be read during review.</li><li>Restore the same pre-review state.</li><li>Rerun with the same issue, spec, and ADW ID, then compare success, issues, severities, screenshots, and summary.</li></ol>
IndyDevDan/book/vol-1-tac/06-let-your-agents-focus.html:496:          <ul><li><strong>Frozen input:</strong> issue, branch commit, spec path, ADW state.</li><li><strong>One changed variable:</strong> exact prompt sentence or model route.</li><li><strong>Observable outputs:</strong> blocker detection, screenshot use, summary, artifact paths.</li><li><strong>Decision:</strong> keep, revert, or gather another run.</li></ul>
IndyDevDan/book/vol-1-tac/06-let-your-agents-focus.html:527:        <p class="section-lead">The review workflow turns a broad instruction—compare the implementation with the specification—into a stateful pipeline with strict types, visual evidence, severity triage, loud parse failure, bounded repair, and issue/PR reporting.</p>
IndyDevDan/book/vol-1-tac/06-let-your-agents-focus.html:538:          <h3>The same shape on both sides of the agent</h3>
IndyDevDan/book/vol-1-tac/06-let-your-agents-focus.html:577:          <p>An <code>R2Uploader</code> is initialized for screenshot hosting. The reviewer runs through <code>/review</code>, which prepares the app, reads the spec and diff, follows critical paths, and returns JSON. The code parses that response into <code>ReviewResult</code>. Screenshots and issue screenshots are uploaded when R2 is configured, public URLs are attached to the result, and review screenshot data is saved back into state for the documenter.</p>
IndyDevDan/book/vol-1-tac/06-let-your-agents-focus.html:763:          <p><code>adw_document.py</code> requires the issue number and ADW ID because documentation depends on prior branch, spec, and review state. It checks out the recorded branch and runs <code>git diff origin/main --stat</code>. When no changes exist, it reports a graceful no-op rather than inventing documentation. When changes exist, it finds the spec and review screenshot directory, then calls one documenter with <code>[adw_id, spec_path, screenshots_dir]</code>.</p>
IndyDevDan/book/vol-1-tac/06-let-your-agents-focus.html:852:          <p><strong>Secondary lesson:</strong> documentation later uses the review screenshots. Because the patch runs after the original review and the review is not rerun on camera, a copied screenshot can be stale. Artifact lineage matters. A complete repair should refresh proof after the fix so documentation describes the final state.</p>
IndyDevDan/book/vol-1-tac/06-let-your-agents-focus.html:1136:        <div class="teach-back"><p>Without notes, teach the chapter as one causal chain:</p><ol><li>Five questions require five focused stages.</li><li>Fresh context prevents cross-stage pollution.</li><li>Committed prompts and state make steps evaluable.</li><li>Typed review turns proof into a governed decision.</li><li>Patch routes a miss through the system instead of your hands.</li><li>Document writes memory and the conditions for retrieving it.</li><li>KPIs reveal where the layer still requires improvement.</li></ol><p class="fine">Expert pass: your listener can predict why the screenshot-blind reviewer passed, locate the prompt-level correction, and explain why conditional docs do not violate minimum context.</p></div>
IndyDevDan/book/vol-1-tac/06-let-your-agents-focus-STATUS.md:62:4. **Artifact lineage:** the course documenter can receive review screenshot references after a patch. Confirm whether a later editorial pass should explicitly require re-review before documentation so copied proof always reflects the final patched state.

