IndyDevDan/book/vol-1-tac/06-let-your-agents-focus.html:385:          <p>The state file shown during planning contains the ADW ID, issue number, branch name, plan file, and issue class. As phases finish, those fields become a compact routing packet. The reviewer can load state, check out the right branch, and find the spec. It does not need the planner’s internal conversation. The course code <em>tries</em> to add <code>review_screenshots</code> to this state, but <code>ADWState.update()</code> filters everything except the five core fields. The documenter therefore falls back to <code>agents/{adw_id}/reviewer/review_img</code> when local screenshots exist. That mismatch is a real state-contract bug, not a sixth field to memorize.</p>
IndyDevDan/book/vol-1-tac/06-let-your-agents-focus.html:467:            <figcaption><span class="frame-card__t">21:45</span>The object fields in the prompt example line up with the Pydantic models, creating a comparable record—though the prompt’s separate “JSON array” instruction contradicts its object example.</figcaption>
IndyDevDan/book/vol-1-tac/06-let-your-agents-focus.html:582:          <p>The next handoff contains an instructive code bug. <code>adw_review.py</code> calls <code>state.update(review_screenshots=…)</code> and logs that the URLs were saved. But <code>ADWState.update()</code> accepts only <code>adw_id</code>, issue number, branch, plan file, and issue class; <code>save()</code> serializes only those fields. The screenshot URLs are silently discarded. <code>adw_document.py</code> then sees no screenshot state and uses its local <code>review_img</code> directory fallback if that directory exists.</p>
IndyDevDan/book/vol-1-tac/06-let-your-agents-focus.html:584:          <aside class="source-note"><strong>Second prompt↔code drift:</strong> <code>review.md</code> says “Return ONLY the JSON array,” then shows a top-level object that <code>ReviewResult</code> expects. The object fields align; the array/object instruction does not. Loud parse failure contains the risk, but the prompt should be repaired.</aside>
IndyDevDan/book/vol-1-tac/06-let-your-agents-focus.html:1164:          <div><dt>ReviewResult</dt><dd>The Pydantic contract containing success, summary, issue list, screenshot paths, and uploaded screenshot URLs.</dd></div>

